WEBVTT

00:03.709 --> 00:05.904
- I have a question.
- Yeah?

00:06.078 --> 00:07.909
How smart do you have to be
to have sex?

00:10.515 --> 00:12.506
- Well, actually...
- Nah, nah, nah!

00:13.685 --> 00:15.516
- Can I, uh...?
- Nah, nah, nah!

00:15.687 --> 00:17.018
- But I was...
- Nah, nah, nah!

00:18.023 --> 00:19.888
- Oh, come on...
- Nah, nah, nah!

00:24.663 --> 00:26.028
Why do you ask?

00:26.198 --> 00:28.723
- Well, Mom's boyfriend's a doctor.
Yeah.

00:28.900 --> 00:30.891
And doctors are supposed
to be smart, right?

00:31.069 --> 00:34.732
Not as smart as they think they are,
but, uh, go ahead.

00:35.240 --> 00:37.299
Well, when I'm in bed
I can hear them in bed.

00:37.476 --> 00:38.773
- Oh, God.
- Oh, boy.

00:38.944 --> 00:40.468
Oh, goodie.

00:42.114 --> 00:44.912
And Mom's always telling him
that he doesn't know what he's doing.

00:47.052 --> 00:49.543
How much do I love this kid?

00:50.155 --> 00:53.556
Don't interrupt, Charlie.
Go on, sweetheart.

00:53.725 --> 00:56.285
So I'm thinking sex must be
a lot harder than I figured.

00:56.461 --> 00:59.089
I mean, she has to tell him
the same thing every night.

01:00.232 --> 01:02.223
- Every night, you say?
- Berta.

01:02.400 --> 01:05.164
You had a semi-annual subscription,
didn't you?

01:06.805 --> 01:08.238
Come on, you guys. Please?

01:09.508 --> 01:11.373
Can't help you.
- Sorry, no.

01:12.677 --> 01:16.078
Look, Jake, it's not that you have to be
particularly smart to have sex.

01:16.248 --> 01:17.943
IN UNISoN:
Yeah, look at your dad.

01:20.252 --> 01:21.810
Jinx, you owe me a Coke.

01:22.854 --> 01:23.912
Think of it this way.

01:24.089 --> 01:27.456
- Suppose you like banana cream pie.
- I do like banana cream pie.

01:27.626 --> 01:29.457
- Well, good.
- Do we have any?

01:30.595 --> 01:32.995
- No.
- Well, then why did you bring it up?

01:33.865 --> 01:35.628
I was trying to tell you about sex.

01:35.801 --> 01:37.632
What does pie have to do with sex?

01:38.770 --> 01:40.965
- Can I jump in?
- No, no, no!

01:41.139 --> 01:44.074
- How about me?
- Excuse me, if I can't talk, you can't talk.

01:44.242 --> 01:46.506
Am I right, Alan?

01:47.012 --> 01:51.142
Anyway, if you don't tell me
you like banana cream pie...

01:51.316 --> 01:54.547
...and I keep bringing something else...
- But I just told you I like it.

01:56.021 --> 01:58.785
You wanna know what kind of pie
your uncle Charlie likes?

01:59.624 --> 02:01.353
- Oh, come on, I wasrt...
- Nah, nah, nah!

02:02.394 --> 02:04.225
- I'm guessing cherry.
- Nah, nah, nah!

02:07.833 --> 02:09.460
Please, I've got this.

02:09.634 --> 02:12.694
You've got squat.

02:12.871 --> 02:16.807
At this rate, the kid's only gonna get
a stiffy at Marie Callender's.

02:16.975 --> 02:19.910
Okay, okay, forget the pie.

02:20.078 --> 02:22.569
Uncle Charlie said "stiffy. "

02:24.516 --> 02:25.983
Yeah, I heard him.

02:26.151 --> 02:29.643
My point is, you don't have to worry about
being smart enough to have sex, okay?

02:30.121 --> 02:31.145
Okay.

02:33.291 --> 02:39.355
In fact, there are times when brains
and imagination are a distinct disadvantage.

02:39.531 --> 02:41.396
Like when you've been
married for 12 years...

02:41.566 --> 02:44.831
...and you're only allowed to do
the same three things over and over again...

02:45.537 --> 02:48.563
...in exactly the same way
and exactly the same order...

02:48.740 --> 02:53.837
...like you're some kind of unthinking
machine or a trained freaking monkey.

02:56.781 --> 03:01.684
Okay, honestly, how much more damage
could we have caused?

03:01.853 --> 03:05.289
I bet monkeys like banana cream pie.

03:38.390 --> 03:39.516
- Hi, honey.
- Hi, Mom.

03:39.691 --> 03:42.660
- What's in the box?
- Banana cream pie.

03:44.663 --> 03:46.597
You bought him a whole pie?

03:46.965 --> 03:49.092
I bought him two pies.

03:49.668 --> 03:50.999
Why would you do that?

03:51.369 --> 03:53.337
It seemed easier than explaining to him...

03:53.505 --> 03:56.497
...that his mother's fiancé
isn't really a sexual moron.

03:57.442 --> 03:59.910
- Oh, hey, Alan.
Herb.

04:00.078 --> 04:02.979
Uh, why is Jake eating pie
in the bathroom?

04:03.148 --> 04:05.343
Not now. Not now.
What are you talking about?

04:06.084 --> 04:08.109
Jake can hear you two in bed.

04:09.120 --> 04:11.816
Oh, God. Oh, God.

04:11.990 --> 04:14.550
He didn't hear that.

04:20.332 --> 04:23.460
Um, what did he say to you?

04:23.835 --> 04:26.360
Well, uh, basically, he's worried
that when he grows up...

04:26.538 --> 04:28.506
...he won't be smart enough to have sex.

04:29.007 --> 04:30.167
Why would he think that?

04:30.342 --> 04:34.335
He hears you giving Herb instructions
like he's a blind guy in a minefield.

04:40.151 --> 04:41.550
You think that's funny?

04:42.320 --> 04:44.185
No.

04:47.692 --> 04:49.557
- Well, I will talk to him.
- No, no.

04:49.728 --> 04:52.356
Trust me, talking only makes it worse.
Charlie and I tried.

04:52.530 --> 04:55.090
- Great, Charlie knows about this?
- That's not the point, Judith.

04:55.266 --> 04:57.291
The point is,
you need to be a little less vocal.

04:57.469 --> 04:58.800
Maybe do what you did with me...

04:58.970 --> 05:01.165
...and smack him on the head
when he goes off course.

05:01.339 --> 05:03.705
She does that too.

05:05.176 --> 05:08.339
Well, um, thank you, Alan.
I will take care of this.

05:14.019 --> 05:16.715
- I'm sorry to dump this on you.
- Oh, that's okay.

05:16.888 --> 05:20.051
I mean, you know, I'm not judging.
I've been in your position.

05:20.225 --> 05:22.785
Well, she only likes the one.

05:25.730 --> 05:28.028
Yeah, yeah. Been there, done that.

05:29.134 --> 05:32.763
Or, ahh, more correctly, been there,
told I was doing that wrong.

05:35.006 --> 05:39.238
Truth is, I, uh, kind of like the instructions.
It takes out all the guesswork.

05:40.345 --> 05:42.745
- Sure, sure.
- I tend to meander when I don't have...

05:42.914 --> 05:45.212
...you know, a game plan.

05:45.383 --> 05:47.374
Well, that's, uh, never a problem
with Judith.

05:47.552 --> 05:50.487
She's the, uh, vince Lombardi
of sexual intercourse.

05:51.523 --> 05:54.549
She did teach me
to play through the pain.

05:56.394 --> 05:59.625
Yeah, tape it up and get back in there.

06:00.632 --> 06:01.656
Say goodbye, Herb.

06:01.833 --> 06:03.733
- Bye.
- Bye.

06:12.811 --> 06:16.372
- Hey.
- Hey, how did it go with Judith?

06:16.548 --> 06:19.176
It was the most awkward
and uncomfortable conversation...

06:19.350 --> 06:21.113
...I've had in my life.

06:21.286 --> 06:24.653
Huh. More awkward than when you were
a kid and had to explain to Mom...

06:24.823 --> 06:28.190
...why you were hiding a slab
of raw liver in your sock drawer?

06:30.095 --> 06:31.926
Okay, the second most awkward.

06:32.430 --> 06:35.661
What about when she found the warm
cantaloupe with a face drawn on it?

06:36.434 --> 06:38.959
All right, it was in the top five.

06:39.137 --> 06:42.664
I mean, it's just unnatural for a guy
to have to tell his ex-wife...

06:42.841 --> 06:45.275
...to pipe down while she's having sex
with another man.

06:45.810 --> 06:49.177
I'll tell you what's unnatural.
The look on that melors face.

06:51.716 --> 06:54.014
Fruit should not look surprised.

07:04.429 --> 07:07.057
- You're the one who gave me that idea.
- I was joking.

07:07.232 --> 07:09.792
You told me it's what the astronauts do.

07:10.802 --> 07:12.929
Oh, right.

07:13.104 --> 07:16.972
That's how I got you to pee
in the Tang jar.

07:18.743 --> 07:24.545
And let's not forget how I convinced you
Mom's douchebag was your air supply.

07:25.850 --> 07:30.549
Yeah, yeah, my breath smelled
like vinegar for two weeks.

07:32.357 --> 07:35.849
Aw, those were innocent times.

07:39.931 --> 07:42.593
EvELYN: Oh, the kitchen appliances
are a little outdated...

07:42.767 --> 07:45.531
...but you people can cook
with your wristwatches now, can't you?

07:46.905 --> 07:51.069
You're funny. You're a funny firecracker.

07:51.709 --> 07:55.611
- Mom?
- Oh, Charlie, say hello to Hiroshi Goto.

07:55.780 --> 07:57.247
Hi.
- Hello.

07:57.415 --> 07:59.679
Uh, Charlie is my number one son.

08:01.085 --> 08:03.383
Yeah, but she treats me like number two.

08:03.555 --> 08:04.886
Oh.

08:05.857 --> 08:08.291
- Mom, can I talk to you for a minute?
- Of course, darling.

08:08.459 --> 08:11.587
Uh, Hiroshi, why don't you go enjoy
the view from the deck.

08:11.763 --> 08:14.095
There's pretty girls playing volleyball
out on the beach.

08:14.265 --> 08:17.029
Oh, I like volleyball.

08:19.437 --> 08:20.768
Here's what you need to know.

08:20.939 --> 08:23.271
He's filthy rich
and looking for a house on the beach...

08:23.441 --> 08:25.306
...and I have nothing to show him.

08:25.777 --> 08:27.711
So you're selling him my house?

08:27.879 --> 08:30.780
Don't worry, I told him you were
going through an ugly divorce.

08:30.949 --> 08:34.077
But before we close escrow,
you'll reconcile with Cheryl...

08:34.252 --> 08:35.810
...and back out of the sale.

08:35.987 --> 08:38.217
Who's Cheryl?

08:38.556 --> 08:41.616
She is a sweet, selfless girl
who worked nights...

08:41.793 --> 08:45.251
...to put you through law school
while you were sleeping with her sister.

08:47.398 --> 08:50.595
I have to string Mr. Goto along
until I have something to show him...

08:50.768 --> 08:52.133
...that actually is for sale.

08:52.303 --> 08:54.897
Oh, I understand.

08:55.073 --> 08:57.564
It's called a bait and switch,
and it's a felony.

08:57.976 --> 09:02.379
Oh, well, look at you
taking the moral high ground.

09:02.547 --> 09:04.981
And with nary a bottle
nor a whore in sight.

09:06.584 --> 09:07.846
Bravo.

09:08.519 --> 09:11.750
Excuse me, why is there
an Asian man on the deck?

09:11.923 --> 09:14.289
- Mom's selling my house.
- Why?

09:14.459 --> 09:16.620
Marital problems.

09:16.794 --> 09:18.921
You cheating bastard.

09:20.298 --> 09:22.766
- Do I have to find another place to live?
- Yes.

09:25.003 --> 09:28.268
Don't worry, sweetheart.
Mommy's just running a little scam.

09:28.439 --> 09:30.430
But feel free to find another place to live.

09:31.609 --> 09:34.009
Anyway, what's new?
How's my grandson?

09:34.412 --> 09:38.542
- Oh, he's fine.
- Oh, come on, Alan, tell her about the pie.

09:40.018 --> 09:42.111
- What pie?
- There's no pie.

09:42.720 --> 09:45.484
- Jake overheard his mother...
- Nah, nah, nah!

09:46.824 --> 09:47.848
It's nothing.

09:48.026 --> 09:51.985
I just had to have a rather embarrassing
conversation with Judith yesterday.

09:52.163 --> 09:54.631
More embarrassing
than when you were 11 years old...

09:54.799 --> 09:57.165
...and I caught you with the dog
and peanut butter?

09:59.737 --> 10:01.500
You went and did that too?

10:02.373 --> 10:06.309
You told me it's what the cowboys did
on a cattle drive.

10:06.477 --> 10:08.911
And I didn't have a cow.

10:10.381 --> 10:13.976
- Is that why you got rid of our dog?
- I couldn't look at him anymore.

10:17.755 --> 10:18.983
Can we move on, please?

10:19.157 --> 10:20.818
I'm sorry, dear. Now, what about Jake?

10:20.992 --> 10:23.153
I loved that dog.

10:23.328 --> 10:27.025
Well, not as much as your brother did.

10:27.665 --> 10:30.498
But go ahead, Alan.
What did you have to talk to Judith about?

10:30.668 --> 10:31.760
Nothing. Forget it.

10:31.936 --> 10:33.369
Oh, come on, Alan.

10:34.138 --> 10:36.265
The dog whisperer here
got all bent out of shape...

10:36.441 --> 10:39.103
...because Jake heard his mother
going at it with her boyfriend.

10:39.277 --> 10:41.006
That's it? He just heard them?

10:41.179 --> 10:44.342
- That's not enough to traumatize him?
- Absolutely not.

10:44.515 --> 10:47.450
- See, Alan, I told you.
- Well, you would know, Charlie.

10:47.885 --> 10:48.909
What do you mean?

10:49.987 --> 10:52.251
- You don't remember?
- Remember what?

10:52.957 --> 10:54.117
Nothing.

10:55.226 --> 10:56.693
I like it.

10:56.861 --> 10:58.556
Of course you do.

10:58.730 --> 11:00.493
Let me show you the master suite.

11:00.665 --> 11:02.599
That's where she caught him.

11:02.767 --> 11:05.031
Ah, cheating bastard.

11:07.739 --> 11:09.206
What am I supposed to remember?

11:09.374 --> 11:12.241
I was the only one that gave that dog
any kind of attention.

11:19.183 --> 11:20.207
No.

11:29.127 --> 11:31.061
I remember.

11:47.979 --> 11:49.241
Charlie?

11:49.414 --> 11:51.109
Yeah.

11:51.282 --> 11:53.079
What are you doing?

11:53.251 --> 11:55.116
Drinking.

11:55.953 --> 11:58.820
Why are you doing it here?

11:58.990 --> 12:01.720
I can't be alone right now.

12:01.893 --> 12:03.258
Okay.

12:03.428 --> 12:05.089
What's going on?

12:06.531 --> 12:09.091
I remembered, Alan.

12:10.001 --> 12:11.161
Remembered what?

12:12.036 --> 12:13.867
I was 8 years old.

12:14.038 --> 12:16.131
It was late at night.

12:16.307 --> 12:19.868
I must've had a bad dream or something
because I walked into Mom's room...

12:20.044 --> 12:21.341
...and I saw them.

12:22.513 --> 12:24.743
Saw who?

12:24.916 --> 12:27.282
Mom and some guy.

12:27.452 --> 12:32.219
They didn't hear me at first, because
the waterbed was making sloshing noises.

12:32.957 --> 12:35.755
At least I hope it was the waterbed.

12:36.194 --> 12:37.593
Oh, yeah.

12:37.762 --> 12:41.027
Mom's waterbed. Remember how we used
to bounce up and down on it...

12:41.199 --> 12:45.829
...playing lumberjack and doing the...?
- Forget the bed. The bed's not important.

12:46.003 --> 12:47.732
Sorry.

12:49.106 --> 12:50.368
Anyway...

12:51.008 --> 12:53.602
...at some point
they realized I was standing there...

12:53.778 --> 12:55.541
...and the guy said to me:

12:55.713 --> 12:58.546
"Don't worry, Speed Racer.
I'm not hurting your mom. "

12:59.450 --> 13:00.542
Speed Racer?

13:01.786 --> 13:03.754
&lt;i>Remember I had
the Speed Racer pajamas?&lt;/i>

13:03.921 --> 13:06.014
Oh, yeah, yeah, our Christmas pajamas.

13:06.190 --> 13:10.889
&lt;i>Yeah, you got Speed Racer
and I got Laverne &amp; Shirley.&lt;/i>

13:11.062 --> 13:14.759
- So typical. L...
- This is not about you, Alan.

13:15.333 --> 13:18.860
This is about a horrible moment in my life
that I completely repressed.

13:19.036 --> 13:22.938
Mom and the man
with the big red mustache.

13:23.574 --> 13:25.405
Oh, God.

13:25.576 --> 13:29.672
I just realized why Yosemite Sam
always made me nauseous.

13:31.916 --> 13:35.352
&lt;i>- And I'll tell you the worst part.
- Worse than Laverne &amp; Shirley pajamas?&lt;/i>

13:36.954 --> 13:40.048
- Alan.
- I am amazed I'm not a raging queen.

13:40.925 --> 13:42.586
We all are.

13:46.731 --> 13:49.825
Anyway, the next morning,
I asked Mom what happened...

13:50.001 --> 13:53.994
...and she said she didn't know what I was
talking about. And when I kept asking...

13:54.171 --> 13:56.571
...she threw a shoe at my head.
- Oh, yeah.

13:56.741 --> 13:59.869
Yeah, the 4-inch heels.
Oh, she was deadly accurate with those.

14:00.044 --> 14:03.605
She could knock a melon out of your hands
from clear across the room.

14:04.415 --> 14:08.010
Will you get your mind out of the produce
section? I've got a problem here.

14:08.185 --> 14:12.281
Come on, Charlie, it happened years ago
and you turned out...

14:12.456 --> 14:13.548
Yeah, you got a problem.

14:14.258 --> 14:15.282
Thank you.

14:16.494 --> 14:18.826
I gotta tell you, it does help me
feel better about Jake.

14:18.996 --> 14:21.226
I mean, you know,
he didn't see anything...

14:21.399 --> 14:24.391
...and at least we haven't been lying
to him about having sex.

14:24.569 --> 14:28.562
No, no, you just taught him
to associate sex with pie.

14:29.607 --> 14:34.510
Hey, at least I didn't talk him into putting
crotchless panties on a Butterball turkey.

14:35.680 --> 14:37.147
Oh, right.

14:37.315 --> 14:40.011
Best Thanksgiving ever.

14:41.085 --> 14:45.818
You told me it's how the Pilgrims
got through the harsh winter.

14:50.528 --> 14:52.428
He's gotta be asleep by now.

14:52.597 --> 14:54.394
He could wake up.

14:54.565 --> 14:56.192
So we'll be quiet.

14:56.367 --> 14:57.959
I can't be quiet.

14:58.135 --> 15:00.296
Come on, please?

15:00.471 --> 15:01.802
Oh, all right.

15:05.142 --> 15:08.168
No, no, not that way.

15:08.346 --> 15:10.576
Slow down.

15:10.748 --> 15:13.216
I'm still awake.

15:16.087 --> 15:19.989
Are you happy?
I may never be happy again.

15:20.558 --> 15:23.356
Mm, pie.

15:29.333 --> 15:34.032
Rose, did you ever suddenly remember
something that you blocked out years ago?

15:34.205 --> 15:36.002
You mean like a repressed memory?

15:36.173 --> 15:39.199
Yeah, you ever had a repressed memory?

15:39.377 --> 15:41.242
I forget.

15:43.581 --> 15:48.041
Get it? Little psychology humor.
Freud was the first one to use it.

15:48.986 --> 15:51.386
- Ha.
- It's much funnier in German.

15:59.664 --> 16:02.497
So, what memory did you repress?

16:03.567 --> 16:05.330
When I was 8...

16:05.503 --> 16:08.802
...I walked in on my mother having sex.
- Interesting.

16:08.973 --> 16:14.240
Interesting? How about devastating,
horrifying, traumatizing?

16:14.412 --> 16:15.606
Wow.

16:15.780 --> 16:18.248
What, was she, like, blindfolded
and tied to a bed...

16:18.416 --> 16:21.579
...while two guys slapped her butt
with Ping-Pong paddles?

16:22.586 --> 16:24.110
No.

16:24.722 --> 16:25.950
Hmm.

16:26.290 --> 16:29.748
Was she riding around on a goat
while an albino midget dripped honey...

16:29.927 --> 16:31.758
No, no.

16:31.929 --> 16:33.328
No.

16:33.497 --> 16:36.591
It was just sex. One mother, one man.

16:36.767 --> 16:37.791
Boring.

16:39.637 --> 16:42.765
Oh, come on, Charlie.
It's not an uncommon occurrence.

16:42.940 --> 16:45.875
I myself have walked in on
many people having sex.

16:46.043 --> 16:47.943
Accidentally?

16:48.312 --> 16:53.147
My point is, you've recovered the memory
and now you can get on with your life.

16:53.851 --> 16:55.785
No, I can't.

16:57.755 --> 17:00.315
What if it's not
the only repressed memory?

17:00.491 --> 17:04.757
What else is lying just below the surface
ready to burst into my consciousness?

17:04.929 --> 17:08.524
Am I gonna wake up remembering my
mother in the shower with my uncle Donald?

17:09.967 --> 17:13.801
Who I suddenly realize
wasrt really my uncle.

17:13.971 --> 17:16.030
Sounds like you don't have
to worry anymore.

17:16.607 --> 17:19.371
Oh, God, it's all coming back.

17:19.543 --> 17:21.841
Uncle Donald, Uncle Steve.

17:22.012 --> 17:24.606
Uncle Jorge.

17:25.649 --> 17:28.174
I bet I wasrt related
to any of those guys.

17:28.352 --> 17:30.183
This is all good, Charlie. Keep going.

17:30.588 --> 17:32.852
- Oh, boy.
- What?

17:33.557 --> 17:36.117
Not only was Aunt Wendy not my aunt...

17:36.293 --> 17:38.989
...but there was no snake bite
on her boob.

17:44.068 --> 17:45.558
Oh, hey, what are you doing here?

17:45.736 --> 17:50.901
Uh, well, we were hoping that...
Actually I was hoping that, ahh, maybe...

17:51.075 --> 17:53.839
He wants me to stay here tonight
so he and Mom can have sex.

17:55.112 --> 17:58.343
Oh, Jake, I'm sure that's not the reason,
right, Herb?

17:58.516 --> 18:00.347
No, that's pretty much it.

18:01.852 --> 18:03.649
Excuse me.

18:03.821 --> 18:04.845
Where are you going?

18:05.022 --> 18:09.118
To tell Mom that her indiscriminate
bed-hopping has scarred me for life.

18:11.095 --> 18:12.687
Jury's still out on me.

18:23.040 --> 18:24.701
&lt;i>EvELYN
What do you want?&lt;/i>

18:25.309 --> 18:26.742
We need to talk.

18:26.911 --> 18:30.176
&lt;i>EvELYN: You should have called first.
I'm a little under the weather.&lt;/i>

18:30.347 --> 18:34.078
Yeah, well, I'm not feeling so great myself.
I've started remembering things.

18:34.251 --> 18:38.051
&lt;i>EvELYN: Well, call the poor girls,
apologize and stop drinking so much.&lt;/i>

18:39.123 --> 18:41.353
No, I'm remembering things about you.

18:41.525 --> 18:43.015
Things from my childhood.

18:45.496 --> 18:46.793
Wait, what are you doing?

18:47.832 --> 18:51.165
You can't even look at me, can you?

18:52.036 --> 18:54.061
&lt;i>EvELYN: I don't care what you think
you remember.&lt;/i>

18:54.238 --> 18:57.730
&lt;i>I was a terrific mother who loved you
even though you were a horrible boy.&lt;/i>

18:57.908 --> 18:58.932
&lt;i>Now go away.&lt;/i>

19:01.679 --> 19:04.239
Mom, this is important.

19:05.482 --> 19:06.506
Mom?

19:08.352 --> 19:12.345
You ruined Yosemite Sam for me.

19:17.027 --> 19:19.154
Dagnabbit, this isn't over.

19:30.040 --> 19:31.735
Oh, God.

19:31.909 --> 19:33.137
EvELYN:
Charlie.

19:33.310 --> 19:36.040
HIRoSHl: Don't worry, slugger.
I'm not hurting your mother.

19:38.616 --> 19:39.640
Whoa!

19:43.787 --> 19:47.223
- Okay, I gotta go if I'm gonna catch my bus.
- Good night, Berta.

19:47.391 --> 19:49.484
Hey, Dad, guess what I found
in Mom's bedroom.

19:49.660 --> 19:52.390
You know what, I'll take a cab.

19:52.930 --> 19:54.955
An empty can of whipped cream.

19:55.499 --> 19:58.161
Whipped cream. No kidding.

19:58.335 --> 19:59.700
And you know what I'm thinking?

19:59.870 --> 20:02.338
- I know what I'm thinking.
- Nah, nah, nah!

20:04.241 --> 20:05.435
What?

20:05.609 --> 20:10.376
Either whipped cream has to do with sex,
or Mom hides pie in her nightstand too.

20:10.547 --> 20:11.844
Hey, a gal can do both.

20:12.016 --> 20:13.506
Nah, nah, nah!

20:14.451 --> 20:15.782
Hey.

20:15.953 --> 20:19.320
- Hey, what happened to you?
- What are you talking about?

20:19.990 --> 20:22.823
- I thought you went to Mom's.
- No.

20:22.993 --> 20:24.290
Then where were you?

20:24.561 --> 20:27.189
- I don't remember.
- What do you mean, you don't remember?

20:27.364 --> 20:31.596
It's called a repressed memory.
Now drop it.

20:37.775 --> 20:43.509
&lt;i>Any one of you lily-livered, bowlegged
varmints care to slap leather with me?&lt;/i>

20:43.681 --> 20:46.844
&lt;i>I'm the hootingest, tootingest,
shootingest...&lt;/i>

20:47.017 --> 20:48.917
&lt;i>...bobtailed wildcat in the West.&lt;/i>

20:50.587 --> 20:57.083
&lt;i>I'm the fastest gun north, south,
east and west of the Pecos.&lt;/i>
